 "notes": {
  "adminNotes": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 1200,
   "page": "admin",
   "text": "Build notes — admin\n\n• Shell: CSS grid [nav | main], h-dvh. ≥1280 full nav (248px); 768–1279 icon rail (84px); <768 bottom tab bar + safe-area padding.\n• Tables: <table> with caption; tablet drops Order + Reason columns; mobile switches to card lists. Rows are clickable, but the reference is the real <button> for keyboard users.\n• Drawer: role=dialog aria-modal, focus trap, Esc closes, focus returns to the row. 600px desktop, 560px tablet, full-screen sheet on mobile.\n• Customer messages: every message renders as a text node only (never innerHTML/markdown), oldest first, with assistant replies muted in between. Tags: 'Used in decision' / 'After decision' / 'Not yet reviewed'. Threads over 4 entries show first + last 2 with 'Show N earlier'. Attachments are file chips, never previews. Injection matches are underlined + tinted AND explained in words, with the message number.\n• Escalation decisions: note ≥10 chars, confirm dialog, then log {by, at, note}. Cancel is the default focus.\n• Policy = typed rules (5 fixed kinds, scoped Refund window). Prose is generated from rules, never edited. Hash = digest of the normalized rules.\n• Validation runs client + server; field errors inline, summary on submit. Duplicate kind+scope is invalid on the later card.\n• Saves use optimistic concurrency (If-Match: base version) → 409 shows the conflict banner and keeps the draft.\n• Revert = new version copying the old rules, marked 'Reverted from vX'; history is append-only.\n• AI review drafts are advisory, generated in the background after the customer is answered; failures never block a decision.\n• Model name on the drawer is a placeholder — show whatever the backend logs.",
   "w": 420,
   "x": 6080,
   "y": 0
  },
